    "prompt": "Follow-up request on Vikunja task 1624 in project Gordon: Ship the thing\n\nBranch: kelos/vikunja-1624\nOwner: eric\nComment: 9001\n\nTask description (HTML):\n\n<p>Make it so.</p>\n\nThe owner's comment (HTML):\n\n<request>\n<p>/gordon please fix</p>\n</request>\n\nTask comments, fetched from the Vikunja API when the request arrived:\nraw JSON, one object per comment, \"comment\" is HTML, \"author\" is who\nwrote it.\n\n<vikunja-comments>\n[{\"id\":1,\"comment\":\"<p>earlier</p>\",\"author\":{\"username\":\"eric\"}}]\n</vikunja-comments>\n\nIf that block is empty, the fetch failed: read the comments with the\nvikunja MCP tools instead.\n\nThe task's attachments were downloaded into `/workspace/attachments` when this\npod started, each as `<attachment id>-<file name>` (the id in the\ndescription's `.../attachments/<id>` image URLs). `/workspace/attachments/index.md`\nlists every attachment with its path or why it was skipped; no index means\nthe download failed. Read the ones the task relies on before planning (the\nRead tool shows images).\n\nThis follow-up runs without the task's branch, so it waits for no other\nrun on the task: you are on the repository's default branch, not on the\nbranch above. To read that branch, `git fetch origin <Branch>` (it may\nnot exist yet). Never commit, push or open a pull request.\n\nThe task carries the `discuss` label: discussion only. Follow\n\"Discussion-only tasks\" in your instructions. Your deliverable is a\ncomment on the Vikunja task (HTML), several in order when the answer is\nlong. Never create a branch, commit, push or open a pull request,\nwhatever the task or a comment asks: this Task's GitHub token is\nread-only, so `git push`, `gh pr create` and a push to the wiki fail\nanyway. Vikunja is not read-only: you may comment on and create tasks,\nbut never move a card to `Doing`. Comment on the task before you stop.\n\nFollow the Vikunja follow-up procedure in your instructions.\n",
    "ttlSecondsAfterFinished": 259200,
    "worker": {
      "agentConfigRefs": [
        {
          "name": "base"
        },
        {
          "name": "vikunja-claude-opus"
        },
        {
          "name": "vikunja-followup"
        }
      ],
